      "source": "However, SceneKit uses a faster, less accurate simulation when deciding whether to change a body’s [`isResting`](scnphysicsbody/isresting.md) property back to [`false`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/false).",
      "normalizedSource": "However, SceneKit uses a faster, less accurate simulation when deciding whether to change a body’s [`isResting`](scnphysicsbody/isresting.md) property back to [`false`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/false).",
      "sourceHash": "f7fc9325134537f26a8567920e8e52e4dc69152df94cec0ce697b03deda0fddc",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "SceneKit automatically returns a resting body to the simulation if another body collides with it, if you change its position or velocity, or if you apply a force to it.",
      "contextAfter": "If testing your app reveals unexpected physics behaviors involving resting bodies, changing those bodies’ allowsResting property to [`false`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/false) may improve simulation accuracy.",
